    "metric_aggregation_clarification": "The headline 'global' metrics (e.g. Test IoU flood = 0.2802, Val IoU flood = 0.2473) are micro-pooled across all valid pixels (TP, FP, FN, TN) across all evaluated chips in the split. Conversely, 'bootstrap_ci' calculates per-chip metrics and evaluates 1000 bootstrap resamples across chips with replacement. Because per-chip IoU gives equal weight to chips with very small flood extents (where minor boundary discrepancies sharply reduce ratio scores), the macro per-chip bootstrap mean (0.1516 test, 0.1384 val) is lower than the pixel-pooled headline IoU.",
    "chip_count_explanation": "Official Sen1Floods11 splits contain 89 validation chips and 90 test chips. Evaluation explicitly skips chips containing 100% nodata labels (label == -1 across all 512x512 pixels), because calculating IoU on zero ground-truth valid pixels is mathematically undefined (0/0 division). There are 3 all-nodata chips in validation and 1 in test, resulting in 86 evaluated validation chips and 89 evaluated test chips."
